<h2>Who is a partner</h2>
<p>Recurring relationship, not a one-off. Targets:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Marketing agencies</strong> that don't build websites themselves (or don't want to). They serve service businesses; clients ask them "do you know a good web person".</li>
  <li><strong>SEO consultants</strong> doing local SEO. Their clients have terrible websites; they need a build partner who won't compete on the SEO work.</li>
  <li><strong>Business coaches / EOS implementers</strong> serving small service businesses. Their clients' websites are often the bottleneck on growth.</li>
  <li><strong>Accountants and bookkeepers</strong> specializing in trades. They see the client's books and know who is ready to invest.</li>
  <li><strong>Lawyers</strong> who do small-business contracts &mdash; the LLC formation lawyer for tradespeople especially.</li>
  <li><strong>Insurance agents</strong> who specialize in tradespeople (commercial liability, E&amp;O for inspectors). Same logic.</li>
  <li><strong>Equipment / supply distributors</strong> serving a single trade vertical. They sometimes have a "preferred contractor" website-recommendation list.</li>
</ul>

