<h2>Outreach pitch (initial email)</h2>
<pre>Subject: A specific idea for [Partner Business]

Hi {first_name},

I run Pikes Peak Web Designs — I build custom-coded websites for
service businesses (HVAC, roofers, plumbers, inspectors, electricians,
landscapers). One person, $0 down, $175/month flat or $4,000 lump-sum.
The detail is at pikespeakwebdesigns.com.

I noticed [specific reason this person is well-suited] and wanted to
introduce myself. I run a small partner program for the business
coaches / agencies / accountants who already serve owners in the trades
I build for. The structure is simple: I pay the referrer when a referred
client signs ($250-$600 depending on volume tier).

If that is interesting, a 20-minute call this month works. If not, no
hard feelings and I will not chase.

— Jon</pre>

<h2>Onboarding a new partner</h2>
<ul class="sop-checklist">
  <li>20-min call to walk through what I build, what kind of client is the right fit, what is NOT a good fit.</li>
  <li>Send the partner kit: 1-page overview, sample audit deliverable, three sample sites, the partner-tracking link they should use for referrals (UTM-tagged).</li>
  <li>Add them to the CRM partner segment.</li>
  <li>Send a short welcome with a $50 thank-you of their choice (Amazon gift card, coffee shop, etc.) for committing to the program.</li>
  <li>Add to the quarterly check-in cadence.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Quarterly partner check-ins</h2>
<p>Every active partner gets a quarterly touch:</p>
<ul>
  <li>1-line "any leads in the queue?" + 1 piece of value (a relevant blog post or audit observation they can share with their clients).</li>
  <li>Update them on agency progress: new samples shipped, any case study they should know about.</li>
  <li>Ask: anything I can do better for the partnership?</li>
</ul>

<h2>Compensation mechanics</h2>
<ul>
  <li>UTM-tagged referral link given to each partner. Form submissions carry the UTM through to the inbox so attribution is automatic.</li>
  <li>Partner is credited when the referred lead signs the agreement.</li>
  <li>Lump-sum: pay 30 days after final invoice clears.</li>
  <li>Monthly: pay the agreed % of months 1-6 on a monthly cadence (so the partner sees recurring revenue, mirroring the client cadence).</li>
  <li>Partner-specific 1099-NEC issued at year-end if total &ge; $600.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Common issues</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Partner forgets I exist.</strong> Quarterly check-in is non-negotiable. Without it the partnership goes dormant.</li>
  <li><strong>Bad-fit referrals.</strong> Partner is sending the wrong audience. Re-onboard with sharper "this is what a good client looks like" examples.</li>
  <li><strong>Disputes on attribution.</strong> Resolve in the partner's favor on the first ambiguity, every time. The relationship is worth more than the disputed payment.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Exit criteria for the program</h2>
<ul>
  <li>8-12 partners maintained at any time.</li>
  <li>Quarterly check-ins logged.</li>
  <li>1-2 booked clients per quarter sourced from the partner program.</li>
</ul>
